  "limitations": [
    "The database transaction makes the internal approval, release, reservation, Run, Step, and audit facts atomic; it cannot make an external provider call atomic. ORCH-08 establishes release and call-start authority only: RUN-05 owns downstream exact delivery replay, durable receipts, retry classification, and recovery. No exactly-once external effect or general compensation workflow is claimed.",
    "Post-call cancellation is best effort: cancellation fences future claims but cannot recall a connector request that already left the process. Cleanup or terminalization of reserved and already-claimed actions remains ORCH-06 and RUN-03 scope.",
    "EffectPlanRequest.requested_by and the stored approval requester remain free-string historical snapshots. ORCH-08 enforces the stored decision and set integrity but does not claim authenticated requester provenance or end-to-end two-person identity issuance.",
    "Release retains the authenticated decision's sealed role and scope snapshot. It detects persisted authority tamper but does not perform live role revocation or identity-directory lookup between decision and release.",
    "Expiry-only renewal preserves the same exact set epoch. Semantic, plan, membership, or proposal-revision change fails closed with full_set_epoch_required; creation, selection, and supersession of a wholly new complete-set epoch remains a later replan seam.",
    "ORCH-08 emits exact per-member action and approval events plus Run and Step transition events, but it does not introduce a distinct authorization-set aggregate audit event or claim the full operator timeline. RUN-06 and AC-14 retain complete timeline and acceptance ownership.",
    "The mapped schema and constraints are present in metadata only. DEL-04 owns Alembic migration revisions plus upgrade, downgrade, and deployed-schema verification.",
    "File-backed SQLite exercises runtime rollback, tamper, replay, and dispatch behavior. PostgreSQL DDL compilation is verified, but PostgreSQL runtime locking and concurrency have not been executed here.",
    "This requirement exposes application and persistence services only. Broader approval APIs, operator UI, and the end-to-end demo remain API, WEB, and DEMO requirement scope."
  ]
